WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.980
Here's the data on Katagiri Honoka's ability

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.440
and the report on what
happened in the dream world.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.660
I'd like to officially question
Asai Kei on behalf of the Bureau.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.490
Regarding his visit to the office
where the written Script is kept.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.870
I want to know who's behind that.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.120
I'll arrange for it.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.290
Yes?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.340
She's telling me to give the phone to you.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.170
She? Who is it?

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.840
A young woman.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.300
She's claiming that she's
the one behind Asai Kei's actions.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.640
Hello, I'm the director
of countermeasures at the Bureau.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.430
Good evening.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.890
I'm sorry, but I can't introduce myself.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.190
Oh, and why is that?

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.440
I have my reasons.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.990
I'd like to negotiate with you.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:54.490
Let's hear it.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.370
Could you stop trying to find out who I am?

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.990
Including asking Asai?

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.250
Of course.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.210
If you simply told me your name,
there wouldn't be any need to ask him.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.880
I'll tell you, then.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.210
I'm the Witch.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.880
The second Witch.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.220
The Witch?

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.840
You can call me the nameless system, if you like.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.470
I have the same ability as her.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.180
That's amazing.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.520
Do you want to negotiate with me now?

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:28.270
If you can promise you'll stop looking for me,
I'll help you in a month.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.440
Why in a month?

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.190
Because you have a plan.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.030
A very big plan.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:39.200
Are you talking about the surprise birthday
party for one of my subordinates?

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.080
I know about that too,
but that's not what I meant.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.830
The plan to erase all the abilities from this town.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:52.460
You're planning to turn these forty years
of abilities into nothing and start over.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.050
I see.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.220
That's more or less true.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.760
Why wouldn't it be?

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.430
I've actually seen Sakurada in that state.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.010
It was pleasant, wasn't it?

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.680
What's your answer?

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.270
If you can see the future,

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.060
do I really need to tell you?

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.320
Sometimes a good conversation involves
confirming a foregone conclusion.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.240
I see, that's very smart.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.110
I'll contact you again.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:22.870
What if we look into your identity by that time?

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.200
I'll pay you back for that somehow.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.210
For example, I'll spoil to your subordinate

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.830
that your birthday present for them
is an extra-large teddy bear.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.380
That'd be a disaster indeed.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.750
Talk to you later then.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.970
You recorded the whole call, right?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:39.970
Of course.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.390
Delete it now.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.890
Are you sure?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.060
Yeah.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.100
It was about private matters.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.230
I understand.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.810
By the way...

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.730
Was what I said just now a lie?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.530
No, it didn't look like one to me.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.990
I see. Thank you.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.410
<i>So after all,</i>

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.200
<i>the desire to erase all abilities
from Sakurada for good</i>

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.080
<i>might be a private matter to me.</i>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.100
Good morning, director.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.720
Ah, morning.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.310
Were you having a particularly nice dream?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.980
No, why?

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.480
You were smiling in your sleep.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.030
That's pretty creepy.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.280
I'll try to avoid that.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.950
There was a call from the
second Witch just a moment ago.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.530
She's saying she wants to
meet you in person and talk.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.990
Wonderful.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.290
Great timing.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.970
Thank you for your report.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.890
How long are you going to—

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:34.730
There's no point!

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.860
Good to see you, Murase.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.650
You're alone? How unusual.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.990
Will you go with me to the gym?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.240
My friend's band is performing.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.450
Didn't know you had friends.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.950
We get along so well
I'd call him my best friend.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.120
Best friend...

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.710
Your jokes are always so hard to understand.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.330
I tell the truth, and the whole truth.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.210
Sure.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:01.710
What about Haruki?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.050
She's reading the script in our classroom.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.880
Our class is doing a play.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.550
Didn't you get the role of Haruki's lover?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.720
Are you okay with that?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.930
Hard to tell.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.140
I've memorized all my lines, though.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.020
That's not what I meant.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.730
Are you okay leaving Haruki alone?

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.270
That's also hard to tell.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.400
I can't do anything to help her.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.570
What do you mean?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:24.940
Shaved Ice
What do you mean?

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.190
In the dress rehearsal...
Shaved Ice

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:29.360
She couldn't smile in the last scene.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.660
More like this.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.410
Actually, where's Asai?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.920
Kei went to see Nakano Tomoki's
band performance.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.960
Aren't you going with him?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.760
I have to practice for the play.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.630
Actually, there's something even more important.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.550
What is it?

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.300
Jeez!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.470
It's a school festival, you know!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.640
The source of the best high school memories!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:58.730
Misora...

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.810
Have you gotten into a fight with Asai?

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.900
No, we're fine.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:07.360
But you know, Misora,
to me it looks like you're avoiding him.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.320
Yes, I am.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.570
Why?

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.620
I sort of feel guilty.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.410
Guilty?

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:19.210
The truth is, I don't have any
right to stand on this stage.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.330
There should have been an audition.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:25.800
There is someone more suitable
for the role of Kei's lover.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:30.680
I'm sure I should have been chosen
only after being compared to her.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.260
Who is that?

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.180
Someone you don't know.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.640
That certainly makes me curious,

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.350
but if it's someone not from our class,
it shouldn't matter for this play, no?

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.940
I guess so.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.730
I'm saying such incoherent things.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.650
Misora... You're smiling right now.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.660
Is this expression fitting?

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:57.410
I'd add just two more tablespoons of happiness.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.920
<i>Our play will start in just an hour.</i>

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.670
<i>I wonder if Haruki will be able to smile.</i>

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:17.180
Haruki finally found the courage
to break out of her fake Eden.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:21.480
She wanted her relationship with you
to be not only about your abilities,

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.350
and, just like you wanted two years ago,

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.820
she felt an emotion close to a normal girl's affection.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.070
She wished to be with you.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.740
<i>I knew about it.</i>

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.490
<i>About Haruki trying to take
a step forward in our relationship.</i>

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:36.700
<i>It's just...</i>

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.530
Haruki,

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.040
did something happen when you met Tyltyl?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.170
No, nothing really.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:49.170
<i>Is our relationship somehow changing from
what we were to each other two years ago?</i>

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.970
<i>No, it's not that.</i>

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.430
<i>I've just never tried to change it.</i>

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:03.230
<i>It's been a peaceful, but equally cruel relationship.</i>

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.480
<i>I've been content with it,
and never had the courage to speak of more.</i>

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:11.860
<i>She's already taken a step forward,
and yet here I am, still standing in place.</i>

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:16.280
<i>I'm sure that's the only reason she can't smile.</i>

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.490
Thank you!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.290
Murase.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.000
Could you do me a favor?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.210
What?

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.550
I want to go to the roof of the south building.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.840
But the roof is off-limits to students...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:39.930
Tomoki.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.930
Do you have a moment?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.060
What is it?

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:48.690
I want you to help me make sure our play
can have a deeply moving ending.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:52.110
Sure, if it's for our class, I'll do anything.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.150
I want you to deliver a few words.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.320
To Haruki?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.150
Yeah.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.320
And one more person.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.660
To Souma Sumire.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.780
In five minutes.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.990
But isn't she...

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.960
Your ability might reach heaven, for all we know.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.250
You think about her too much.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.000
Please, Tomoki.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.710
It's a kind of ritual for me.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:19.760
Just like exchanging rings only after
you swear eternal love before God.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.260
I see. Okay, I'll do it.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.480
Have you prepared a cool line?

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.310
I don't need any cool lines.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.520
I'll just tell the truth.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.150
Sure, let's do this.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.940
Hey, Souma!

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:39.530
From your perspective,

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.910
it's a message from 5 minutes ago,
October 22nd, 1:43 PM.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.540
It's been already two years
since you went to heaven.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.460
Quite a while, don't you think?

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.250
Are you okay up there?

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.090
Kei has something he wants to talk to you about.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.300
Listen to him, please.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.130
Here we go.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.170
Passing the mic to our hero, Asai Kei!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.430
I'm going to the south building's roof.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:07.220
I'll be there for the first time in two years,
one month, and twenty one days.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.140
And I'll meet Haruki Misora there.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:13.310
Souma, I'll definitely put an end to that summer.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:15.820
Haruki.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.030
I want you to come to the roof of the south building.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:52.980
Come closer.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:56.150
How close should I get?

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.730
Closer. Until you're right in front of me.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:09.620
There's something I need to apologize to you about.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.960
What is it?

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.670
It's about Souma Sumire.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.130
I'm sorry.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.210
I'm sorry.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.840
I don't like Souma Sumire.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:27.010
I've wished many many times she wasn't there.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.850
I've wished she hadn't come back from that picture.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.520
I'm sorry, Kei.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.270
I'm selfish.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:41.990
I'm scared my reset ability will lose
its value because of Souma Sumire.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.990
Yeah, I know.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.740
<i>As we live, it often so happens
that we come to dislike people.</i>

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.200
<i>Yet you don't avert your eyes.</i>

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.040
<i>That's why you end up deeply troubled,
more than necessary.</i>

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:59.170
<i>And so, embracing every feeling in your heart
without deceiving yourself, you feel guilt,</i>

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.880
<i>which I find extremely beautiful.</i>

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.920
<i>Our abilities are what brought us together.</i>

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:07.720
<i>Because we have them, we automatically,
as if it was the most natural thing,</i>

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.850
<i>were always together.</i>

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.480
You know, Haruki.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.690
Haruki...

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:20.570
Even if we didn't have our abilities,
I'd still want to spend time with you.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.860
I want to know what you find beautiful
and share those feelings with you.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:30.030
I want to spend time with you, sharing memories
of the same places, the same things.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:40.290
So, Haruki, I hope we'll spend
plenty of time together.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.770
Everything, all of it, exactly as I'd planned!

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.900
<i>You're so unfair.</i>

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.230
<i>You're the only one who doesn't suffer.</i>

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:08.200
<i>Pretending it's for Kei's sake, you escape
into a position where only you don't get hurt.</i>

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.410
<i>All the pain is forced onto me.</i>

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.950
<i>You're the only one who has it easy.</i>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:19.210
<i>I'm already too tired of this.</i>

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:21.500
<i>But...</i>

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.050
<i>Just a bit more...</i>

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.350
Haruki, we should save.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.890
Why is that?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:40.100
I don't want to reset what happened today.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:42.860
I see.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.190
Save.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.320
Sunday
October 22nd
Save.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.320
October 22nd
Sunday

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.710
Say, Souma.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:04.170
If you're seeing this future,
could you appear in front of me?

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:09.970
I also want to see you, but I can't right now.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.430
Anyway, congratulations.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.140
Is this a happy end?

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.010
It's a bit early for an ending.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.430
But yeah.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.440
I'm really happy.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:24.310
You hurt me with your words
without a care in the world.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:27.190
I can't imagine a lie that you wouldn't see through.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.440
That's too bad.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.570
I'd let you deceive me all you want.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.950
I need you to do me a favor.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.000
I'll do anything, as long as it's in my power.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.210
I'd like to hear why you want me to do it, though.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.790
I'll tell you once everything is over.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.330
Absolutely everything...

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.170
Tomorrow, go pick up trash with Haruki.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.920
You'll start at 9 AM.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.920
Do it at Shikanokami intersection.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:53.930
I'll tell the school that we caught a cold.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:56.010
Thanks. And sorry for making you do this.

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:58.770
It'll be the end soon, though.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.890
In a few days, everything will be over.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.440
I'll contact you again.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.650
Hey, Kei.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.990
Hi, Tomoki.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.910
A message just reached me.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.080
All I can think of is your ability.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.750
Any ideas?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.540
No, not that I recall.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.420
I see.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.050
Whose message did I deliver?

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.510
Are you the second Witch?

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.260
That's right, nice to meet you.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.600
She's not lying.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.140
She has the ability to see through lies.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.730
I know.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.150
It's been a month and, like we agreed,

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:50.570
we haven't investigated into your identity at all.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.030
I'll cooperate.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:54.320
Thank you.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:59.080
Why are you hiding your ability from the Bureau?

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.750
I don't want people controlling me.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:05.000
You wouldn't want to become
like the Witch, would you?

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.880
And yet you were the one who contacted me first.

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:11.090
It's because you're not the Bureau.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.840
You're working towards a more personal goal.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:18.640
That's why you keep the existence
of a second Witch secret.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.140
The Bureau still doesn't know about me.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:25.890
Are you trying to say that
the Bureau is our common enemy?

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:29.820
Should someone working for
the Bureau really call it his enemy?

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.820
It's not a problem, no one's listening.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.030
How so?

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.410
It's physically impossible.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.460
Let me introduce you. This is Kagaya.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.630
Anything he touches with his right hand is locked.
It stops undergoing any changes.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.670
You seem quite surprised.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:54.840
That's so strange.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.510
Shouldn't you already know everything?

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.720
That's such a mean question.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:02.140
Isn't it exactly according to your plan?

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.770
It means you couldn't see this future.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.270
That's right.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:10.060
My ability doesn't work on you.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:15.740
My clairvoyance allows me to peek into the
future memories of the person I'm talking with.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.660
And you're dealing with it in such an abnormal way.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.120
Your ability lets you erase memories.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:26.500
You're disposing of your own
memories at fixed intervals.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.830
If your future self doesn't have any memories,

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.880
my ability won't activate.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.670
What a discernment.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.840
My memories are full of holes, as if eaten by moths.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:41.090
Living with just one little notebook
serving as your memory

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.470
is definitely unthinkable.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.970
It's not one notebook.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.140
It's two.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:47.680
I use them to deal with resets.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.230
If Kagaya always keeps one locked,

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.690
I can keep information even if a reset happens.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.570
Let's continue, though.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.400
I need to ask you something.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.530
What is it?

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.820
The second Witch...

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.450
Will my plan succeed?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.580
Your plan will indeed succeed.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:11.080
I'm seeing that future right now.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.880
One more question.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.710
Will you try to foil my plan?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.630
No, I won't do anything.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:23.470
I want all abilities to disappear
from this town as soon as possible.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.720
Neither of her answers was a lie.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.230
"Will you try to foil my plan?"
"Will my plan succeed?"

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.270
It's set in stone now.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:34.820
The moment a future-seer
answered those two questions,

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.440
the words gained an absolute meaning.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:41.320
My plan will definitely succeed.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:49.960
Kei.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:54.420
Why did Souma Sumire instruct us to pick up trash?

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.550
I have absolutely no idea.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.880
We'll have to just do as we're told, though.

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:02.510
But Souma Sumire made a mistake two years ago.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:05.470
What mistake was that?

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:08.720
Do you think her dying was the right thing to do?

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:10.430
You have a point.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.730
Right, that was a mistake.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:15.560
When it comes to Souma Sumire,

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.360
I feel like you get a bit less composed.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.990
You may be right.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.570
I'll keep that in mind.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:24.360
Why don't we take a break?
Do you want anything to drink?

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.660
Yes.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.410
Please stay here.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.080
I'll go buy something to drink.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:42.760
<i>I can't direct my sight at it!</i>

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:55.150
Did you see the accident happen?

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.020
No,

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.060
I heard the collision,

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.150
but for some reason, I couldn't look in its direction.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:02.530
The same as me.

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.200
I see, okay.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.990
I'll look into it too.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.200
How strange.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.870
Why was Asai at the scene of the collision?

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.370
Did you tell him to be there?

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.290
No.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.750
I didn't tell him anything.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.510
She's not lying.

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:23.840
Whatever.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:26.720
Actually, I want to ask you to do something for me.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.350
What is it?

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:31.520
Could you join the Bureau's
countermeasures department?

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.520
There won't be any casualties. Don't worry.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.150
Here's my next request.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:46.910
At 3 PM, go do some shopping in the
supermarket near Nanasaka Middle School.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:50.330
Carrots, onions, chicken.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.700
And a yogurt.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.830
<i>A yogurt?</i>

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.960
Until next time.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.460
Next Episode

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.090
If you think about it, it's not that big of a case.

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:01.710
How will the Bureau deal with it?

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:03.340
You really should rest.

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:04.630
Maybe it's because I'm in the Bureau.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:06.340
Was such a stupid reason really worth it?

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:07.550
Well, Kei.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.760
It's time for the next request.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:21.360
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:27.570
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:33.830
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:43.420
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:47.880
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:50.260
You get lost while searching for

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:54.140
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:57.060
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:00.020
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:00.480
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.110
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:06.150
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:09.320
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:12.950
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:15.450
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:17.200
If it were so simple to just

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:20.210
Lock your own heart

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:23.340
How lovely life would be

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:28.590
But I believe you have the key

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:34.930
To let my soul be free
